@startuml
' Evidence: Laplace-UCI/src/Laplace.Uci/Connections.cs SHA256 804a8785d1e69fd88ab4d3e519c50754ad2408b1767a2c3b12975bb32d30cbd4
' Evidence: Laplace-UCI/src/Laplace.Uci/Configuration.cs SHA256 dfeae8c31a84cff881907434d1cba900c45d12f74141171c6c50daffe214ecca
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFCFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
title UCI connector — transport opening
start

if (WebSocket profile?) then (yes)
 :Create ClientWebSocket;
 :Read token; set Bearer header and 15-second keepalive interval/timeout;
 :Link cancellation and configured connection deadline;
 :Connect to configured endpoint;
 if (Exception?) then (yes)
  :Dispose socket; rethrow;
  stop
 endif
 :Return bounded WebSocket connection;
else (process or ssh)
 :Construct ProcessConnection;
 :Disable shell execution; redirect stdin/stdout/stderr; hide window;
 if (SSH?) then (yes)
  :Set batch mode, strict host-key checking and connect timeout;
  :Pass configured host; quote configured executable/arguments for remote exec;
 else (local process)
  :Resolve selected executable; append argument list; set working directory;
  :Load environment files in order;
  :Apply variable overrides or removals;
 endif
 :Start process; fail if no process returned;
 :Wrap stdout/stdin as bounded text connection;
 :Pump diagnostic stderr to connector stderr;
 :Return process connection;
endif
stop
footer
Source-reviewed orchestration. Nested semantics remain open; no runtime acceptance
claimed. Process/SSH constructor does not take the OpenAsync cancellation token. SSH
timeout is passed to ssh; WebSocket uses a linked deadline. HTTP callers select a
configured profile, not arbitrary executable arguments. No engine process or connector
endpoint was started.
end footer

@enduml
